Package: curatedMetagenomicData
Title: Curated Metagenomic Data of the Human Microbiome
Version: 4.0.1
Date: 2026-04-18
Description:
    The curatedMetagenomicData package provides standardized, curated 
    microbiome data for novel analyses. Starting with version 4 ("cMD4"),
    sample-level profiling data is served from a published DuckDB catalog over
    Hive-partitioned Parquet files produced by the curatedMetagenomicDataETL 
    pipeline.
 .
      Hive-partitioning (organizing a dataset across many files by encoding
    column values into the directory path itself, rather than storing those
    values inside the files) lets the catalog skip files that don't match 
    sample-side filters. Parquet's columnar layout reads only the requested 
    features from the fiels that remain, and DuckDB coordinates these 
    operations through a single queryable catalog. Together, these let users 
    load only the samples and features of interest without downloading full 
    study datasets.
 .
      Sample metadata is shipped directly with the package as two data.frame 
    objects; harmonized_meta (curated schema columns only) and all_meta 
    (harmonized schema plus under-harmonization columns), both derived from
    `curatedMetagenomicDataCuration::makeCombinedMetadata()`. The runtime
    package itself does not depend on curatedMetagenomicDataCuration. Users
    filter harmonized_meta or all_meta to samples of interest and call
    returnSamples() to obtain a SummarizedExperiment assembled across studies
    on demand.
